// Title: Triple Cross eBPF Rootkit Execve Hijack
// Sigma ID: 0326c3c8-7803-4a0f-8c5c-368f747f7c3e
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth
// Description: Detects execution of a the file "execve_hijack" which is used by the Triple Cross rootkit as a
//   way to elevate privileges
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/h3xduck/TripleCross/blob/1f1c3e0958af8ad9f6ebe10ab442e75de33e91de/src/helpers/execve_hijack.c#L275
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_triple_cross_rootkit_execve_hijack.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/sudo" and ProcessCommandLine contains "execve_hijack"
